course: dictionary
lesson: 2307
title: Criticism: saying what could be better
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Criticism is saying what is wrong or bad about someone or something. It is not always rude. When a coach tells you what to fix, that is criticism too. «Coaches say criticism helps in practice, not at the starting line.» Before a show, they encourage you. After it, they talk about getting better.
explain: The best criticism is kind and specific. It names one thing and suggests a way to improve. «I love the colours, maybe make the dog bigger?» starts with something good, then gives one clear idea. Saying «Your drawing is rubbish» is criticism too, but it is not helpful, because it does not say what to change.
explain: A criticism is one point about what is wrong. When people criticise a plan, they point out its problems. «The plan faced criticism» in the news means people said what was wrong with it. Writers, artists and musicians also get criticism from critics, who judge their work.
fact: Criticism means saying what is wrong or bad about someone or something.
fact: A criticism is one single point about what is wrong.
fact: «Constructive criticism» is criticism that helps you improve.
fact: In a formal sense, «criticism» can mean judging books, art or music, as in «literary criticism».
fact: Saying «No offence, but...» before a criticism does not stop the words from hurting, so be kind and specific.
exercise: «Coaches say criticism helps in practice.» What does criticism mean here? | Cancelling the practice | Cheering loudly for every goal | *Telling someone what they could do better | Shouting at the team until they cry
exercise: «I love the colours, maybe make the dog bigger?» Which part is the criticism, the point about what is wrong? | I love the colours | *Maybe make the dog bigger | Both parts are rude | The dog is a cat
exercise: Ella's teacher gave her three criticisms of her poem. What is one criticism? | A whole new poem written by the teacher | *One point about what could be better | A prize for her poem | A copy of the poem in a book
test: «The plan faced criticism.» What does this tell you? | People all agreed the plan was perfect | *People said what was wrong with the plan | The plan was cancelled by the weather | People danced in the street for the plan
test: Literary criticism means judging books. What is literary criticism? | Telling a story out loud | Making a book out of paper | A list of the best books to buy | *Judging books, art or music
exam: Which sentence is an example of kind, helpful criticism? | «Stop drawing forever.» | «Your drawing is rubbish.» | *«I love the colours, maybe make the dog bigger?» | «No offence, but you cannot draw.»
